  "question": {
    "text": "Consider a pyramid<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi></math> located in the first octant <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>y</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>z</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> with<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi></math>, as origin, and<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi><mi>P</mi></math> and,<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi><mi>R</mi></math> along the&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8208;</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>s</mi></math> and the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>&#8208;</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>s</mi></math>, respectively. The base<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi></math> of the pyramid is a square with<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi><mi>P</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn></math>. The point S is directly above the mid-point T of diagonal,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi><mi>Q</mi></math>,&nbsp; such that,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mi>S</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn></math>. Then&nbsp;"
  },
